Day 41: Extravagant Love | Monday of Holy Week (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
Mary kneels before Jesus.
She breaks open the jar.
She pours it out completely.
Extravagant love.

Welcome to Day 41 of our Lent journey, the first full day of Holy Week.
Today’s reflection brings you into one of the most intimate, breathtaking moments in the Gospels — Mary anointing Jesus with costly perfume, offering Him the most precious thing she has because He is the most precious One she knows.

This spoken‑word devotional invites you into that same posture of wholehearted devotion. Holy Week is not a time for halfway love. It is a time for sincerity, vulnerability, and offering Jesus something real — your time, your attention, your trust, your heart.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why Mary’s act of devotion is shocking in its sincerity

How Holy Week invites you to offer Jesus your own costly love

Why extravagant love is measured by the heart, not the size of the offering

A prayer to love Jesus with generosity and truth

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Jesus, this is for You.”

